ion without response')) [adapters.py:send:498] [http.py:get_downloader_session:506]]\n\n- download_url(error): /data/project/rehab_eNKI/eNKI_data/ (file) [Access to https://dx-download.trendscenter.org/dataDownloadCenter/?c=fca2a2800192704%7C91008\u0026e=simon.b.eickhoff@gmail.com has failed: status code 502 [http.py:check_response_status:116]]\n\n- download_url(error): /data/project/rehab_eNKI/eNKI_data/ (file) [Access to https://dx-download.trendscenter.org/dataDownloadCenter/?c=ff684e7bc17f216%7C91308\u0026e=simon.b.eickhoff@gmail.com has failed: status code 504 [http.py:check_response_status:116]]\n\n\nAdditional Information:\nMy first thought was, that the authentification might be \"broken\" for the urls after some time. But if I delete a file, that I could download, I can download it again, so the links are not expired.\n\nI checked a few archives that I could download, they contain for example niftis, that I could open \"normally\". But I am not aware of a possibility to check, if the data might be not complete or even has errors in it.\n\n@mih","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579189683,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDMzODk3NDI4MQ=="},"target":"623eee1216926514fb642799519b6914a45202f2ca35253b3656e444fdccaba7","message":"Hey, \nI am at the moment trying to download the eNKI-dataset from https://coins.trendscenter.org/ \nI can log in on that page, go there on \"download\" and then I get either a list of ~500 zips, that I can click on and my browser wants to download that.\n\nAt the end of the list of zips, I can get also a list of ~500 urls, that lead to the download.\nExample: \"https://dx-download.trendscenter.org/dataDownloadCenter/?c=582eb1e0f2ba9f5|91401\u0026e=???@gmail.com\"\nSo my plan was, to iterate over this list of urls (that I copied into a textfile) with datalad download-url, which works for ~100 of the 500 files.\n\nFor the rest I get a set of different errors:\n\n- download_url(error): /data/project/rehab_eNKI/eNKI_data/ (file) [Downloaded size 681181184 differs from originally announced 5262639843 [base.py:_verify_download:351]]\n\n- download_url(error): /data/project/rehab_eNKI/eNKI_data/ (file) [Failed to establish a new session 1 times. Last exception was: ('Connection aborted.', RemoteDisconnected('Remote end closed connection without response')) [adapters.py:send:498] [http.py:get_downloader_session:506]]\n\n- download_url(error): /data/project/rehab_eNKI/eNKI_data/ (file) [Access to https://dx-download.trendscenter.org/dataDownloadCenter/?c=fca2a2800192704%7C91008\u0026e=???@gmail.com has failed: status code 502 [http.py:check_response_status:116]]\n\n- download_url(error): /data/project/rehab_eNKI/eNKI_data/ (file) [Access to https://dx-download.trendscenter.org/dataDownloadCenter/?c=ff684e7bc17f216%7C91308\u0026e=???@gmail.com has failed: status code 504 [http.py:check_response_status:116]]\n\n\nAdditional Information:\nMy first thought was, that the authentification might be \"broken\" for the urls after some time. But if I delete a file, that I could download, I can download it again, so the links are not expired.\n\nI checked a few archives that I could download, they contain for example niftis, that I could open \"normally\". But I am not aware of a possibility to check, if the data might be not complete or even has errors in it.\n\n@mih","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579189988,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDMzODk3Nzk3MA=="},"target":"623eee1216926514fb642799519b6914a45202f2ca35253b3656e444fdccaba7","message":"Hey, \nI am at the moment trying to download the eNKI-dataset from https://coins.trendscenter.org/ \nI can log in on that page, go there on \"download\" and then I get either a list of ~500 zips, that I can click on and my browser wants to download that.\n\nAt the end of the list of zips, I can get also a list of ~500 urls, that lead to the download.\nExample: \"https://dx-download.trendscenter.org/dataDownloadCenter/?c=secret\u0026e=???@gmail.com\"\nSo my plan was, to iterate over this list of urls (that I copied into a textfile) with datalad download-url, which works for ~100 of the 500 files.\n\nFor the rest I get a set of different errors:\n\n- download_url(error): /data/project/rehab_eNKI/eNKI_data/ (file) [Downloaded size 681181184 differs from originally announced 5262639843 [base.py:_verify_download:351]]\n\n- download_url(error): /data/project/rehab_eNKI/eNKI_data/ (file) [Failed to establish a new session 1 times. Last exception was: ('Connection aborted.', RemoteDisconnected('Remote end closed connection without response')) [adapters.py:send:498] [http.py:get_downloader_session:506]]\n\n- download_url(error): /data/project/rehab_eNKI/eNKI_data/ (file) [Access to https://dx-download.trendscenter.org/dataDownloadCenter/?c=secret\u0026e=???@gmail.com has failed: status code 502 [http.py:check_response_status:116]]\n\n- download_url(error): /data/project/rehab_eNKI/eNKI_data/ (file) [Access to https://dx-download.trendscenter.org/dataDownloadCenter/?c=secret\u0026e=???@gmail.com has failed: status code 504 [http.py:check_response_status:116]]\n\n\nAdditional Information:\nMy first thought was, that the authentification might be \"broken\" for the urls after some time. But if I delete a file, that I could download, I can download it again, so the links are not expired.\n\nI checked a few archives that I could download, they contain for example niftis, that I could open \"normally\". But I am not aware of a possibility to check, if the data might be not complete or even has errors in it.\n\n@mih","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1579191788,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NTIyOTk5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3#issuecomment-575229992"},"message":"\u003e So my plan was, to iterate over this list of urls (that I copied into a textfile) with datalad download-url, which works for ~100 of the 500 files.\n\nwhy not to try using `datalad addurls`?\n\n502 == bad gateway, 504 == gateway timeout...   Can you download those particular ones nicely using browser?  what would be the size? any errors reported in the console?  is initial size reported matches what ends up being downloaded?   I could hypothesize on what possibly could go wrong, but better to get more \"information\" first.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"5251a8cf1239b834eec2d241c5de46425d3a2cbe"},"timestamp":1579247604,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NTUxNDcwOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3#issuecomment-575514709"},"message":"I choosed \"datalad download_url\" because it worked for downloading the first archive via error, so I ran that in parallel for all links. I will also try datalad addurls.\n\nAfter downloading and comparing the sizes for two archives with du :\n8247640 via browser, but\n8243934 via datalad download-url\n\n6036660 via browser\n5856524 with datalad download-url\n\n``\n\u003e datalad download-url \u003curl\u003e\ndownload_url(ok): /data/project/rehab_eNKI/eNKI_data/scan_data003.zip (file)\nadd(ok): scan_data003.zip (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  download_url (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n``\n\nThe console does not report errors. I restarted the download another time over night and got 30 new archives without error messages in the console or the log-files. The example scan_data003.zip\n\u003e unzip scan_data003.zip\nworks without error messages, but these archives are probably all not complete.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"5251a8cf1239b834eec2d241c5de46425d3a2cbe"},"timestamp":1579247604,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDMzOTM5NTc4NA=="},"target":"1af87f97f9568f1f9747c6b5db0efab132a90f4a3be4f522250b6b1a6b2e85f4","message":"I choosed \"datalad download_url\" because it worked for downloading the first archive via error, so I ran that in parallel for all links. I will also try datalad addurls.\n\nAfter downloading and comparing the sizes for two archives with du :\n8247640 via browser, but\n8243934 via datalad download-url\n\n6036660 via browser\n5856524 with datalad download-url\n\n``\n\u003e datalad download-url \u003curl\u003e\ndownload_url(ok): /data/project/rehab_eNKI/eNKI_data/scan_data003.zip (file)\nadd(ok): scan_data003.zip (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  download_url (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n``\n\nThe console does not report errors.\n\u003e unzip scan_data003.zip\n\nworks without error messages, but these archives are probably all not complete. \n\nRestarting the download for all missing archives gives ~30 archives that before gave error messages.\nThe logs for the ones that are still missing contain the errors from above.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1579270874,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NTY0NDk4Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3#issuecomment-575644987"},"message":"so it feels like we have a bug! :-(  Let's continue in https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4042 and please cut/paste there output from `datalad wtf -D html_details`.  I will try to get to it next week unless someone beats me to it.  Troubleshooting access to a closed-source (although loudly stated/promised to be open) platform is not on my priority list.","files":null}]}